      ▼               ▼
 eventApi         authApi
      │               │
      ▼               ▼
 request.js       request.js
      │
      ▼
 Flask API


 all services share the same request.js.

 So if later we need:
- authorization headers
- access tokens
- refresh tokens
- global 401 handling
- request IDs
- logging
- retry logic
- CSRF handling
- error normalization
we change the central request layer rather than 30 API files.
That's exactly what we want for a production-style application.



